# Tracer: a tuple equality must not shadow the function's Cartesian codomain.
# Before: with the vec equality below, the final dot expansion failed.
# vec(a,b) = (b[1]-a[1],b[2]-a[2])
# dot(vec(a,b),vec(a,b)) = vec(a,b)[1]*vec(a,b)[1] + vec(a,b)[2]*vec(a,b)[2]
# The tuple-shape reader returned TupleEquality, whose cart() was None,
# before reading the existing function codomain. Residual equality WD failed.
# Now: carrier-bearing evidence is tried before dimension-only fallback.
have fn vec(A,B cart(R,R)) cart(R,R) = (B(1)-A(1),B(2)-A(2))
have fn dot(u,v cart(R,R)) R = u(1)*v(1)+u(2)*v(2)
have a,b cart(R,R)
vec(a,b) = (b(1)-a(1),b(2)-a(2))
vec(a,b)(1) = b(1)-a(1)
vec(a,b)(2) = b(2)-a(2)
dot(vec(a,b),vec(a,b)) = vec(a,b)(1)*vec(a,b)(1) + vec(a,b)(2)*vec(a,b)(2)
# Boundary: out-of-range projections and incompatible signatures still reject.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_known_special_property/fn_tuple_carrier_after_equality.lit
